      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "TextEncodeQwenImage21"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Task: Redraw a very small classic fantasy RPG sprite as newly illustrated high resolution art. Reconstruct plausible missing detail; do not enlarge or trace the pixel blocks.\n\nInput image: costume, silhouette and colour-blocking reference. Preserve the classic figure's proportions, neckline, garment overlap and major colour regions while squaring into a clean symmetrical 30-degree wide-A turnaround pose with empty open hands. \n\nSubject and composition: A medieval Daggerfall battle-mage in weathered dark teal hooded robes over a belted grey tunic, dark trousers and sturdy leather boots, with a stern shadowed face visible inside his hood. Shown full-length as the front view of a costume fitting or character turnaround sheet, in a symmetrical neutral standing A-pose facing directly forward, feet slightly apart with both shoes/feet whole. Both arms are held out at a wide 30-degree A-pose well away from his sides, leaving a wide clear gap of background between each arm, hand and his waist/pouches; hands open and empty (no weapon or staff). \n\nStyle: ART DIRECTION \u2014 VAGRANT STORY & OLD TABLETOP DARK FANTASY PEN-AND-INK CROSSHATCHING WITH MUTED WASH\n\nDraw the character as an accomplished pen-and-ink dark-fantasy character sheet in the tradition of Akihiko Yoshida (Vagrant Story) and classic tabletop RPG manuals, finished with opaque muted gouache washes. Build a confident underlying ink drawing with crisp seams, dark-umber contours, fine directional crosshatching inside folds, and opaque local colour washes preserving the sprite's exact colour relationships without glossy 3D shading.\n\nPresentation: Full-length isolated figure filling ~88% of the vertical portrait frame on a perfectly flat solid dark slate grey background, RGB 48,52,59. Soft overhead light equal on both sides. No floor, no cast shadow, no border.",
        "",
        1024
      ]
    },
