      "widgets_values": [
        "Painting style of Larry Elmore, Brom style, gothic fantasy illustration, dark_fantasy_illustration.\n\nDrawn and painted as a vivid, punchy 1990s PC fantasy role-playing game character sheet: confident dark-umber pen-and-ink contour lines, fine crosshatching only inside cloth folds and overhangs equally on both sides, and opaque matte gouache colour planes (4 to 6 painted value groups per material). Plain flat dark slate-grey background, RGB 48,52,59, no floor or border.\n\nSubject and composition: A medieval Daggerfall battle-mage in weathered dark teal hooded robes over a belted grey tunic, dark trousers and sturdy leather boots, with a stern shadowed face visible inside his hood. Shown full-length as the front view of a costume fitting or character turnaround sheet, in a symmetrical neutral standing A-pose facing directly forward, feet slightly apart with both shoes/feet whole. Both arms are held out at a wide 30-degree A-pose well away from his sides, leaving a wide clear gap of background between each arm, hand and his waist/pouches; hands open and empty (no weapon or staff). "
      ]
